"""
frz - a Gemini-CLI-style multi-provider chat client for the terminal.

Features:
  - Four provider protocols: Anthropic (Claude) / OpenAI / Google Gemini /
    OpenAI Responses API
  - Pure standard library (urllib); no third-party dependency required
  - Terminal Markdown rendering (headings/bold/lists/tables/code blocks);
    install pygments for syntax highlighting in code blocks
  - Hand-drawn ASCII box diagrams (┌─┐ │ └─┘) in code blocks are automatically
    realigned, fixing ragged right edges caused by the model miscounting CJK width
  - Sessions can be saved / resumed / listed / exported to Markdown,
    stored in ~/.frz/sessions/*.json
  - REPL slash commands: /help /save /rename /resume /list /new /export /edit
    /system /model /baseurl /history /clear /exit
  - REPL input comforts: Tab completion (commands & session names), /edit for
    multi-line input in $EDITOR, /history with automatic paging,
    /resume without a name resumes the most recent session

Usage examples:
  # Start a new session (defaults to Anthropic claude-sonnet-4-6)
  frz --api-key sk-ant-xxxx

  # Pick a provider / model
  frz --provider openai --model gpt-4o --api-key sk-xxxx

  # Provide the key via environment variable (keeps it out of shell history)
  export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxx
  frz

  # Resume a previous session
  frz --resume my-session

  # List all saved sessions
  frz --list-sessions

  # Persist default provider/model/api-key so you don't have to pass them again
  frz config set --provider anthropic --model claude-sonnet-4-6 --api-key sk-ant-xxxx

  # Talk to a Responses-API service (e.g. Volcengine Ark) with true streaming output
  export ARK_API_KEY=ark-xxxx
  frz --provider openai_responses --model kimi-k3 \\
      --base-url https://ark.cn-beijing.volces.com/api/v3
  # base-url/model can also be persisted; afterwards --provider openai_responses is enough
  frz config set --provider openai_responses \\
      --model kimi-k3 --base-url https://ark.cn-beijing.volces.com/api/v3 --api-key ark-xxxx
"""

